            <ArticleTitle>Invasive group G streptococcal infection in a paediatric patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr2016217790</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2016-217790</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a paediatric case of group G streptococcal bacteraemia and vertebral osteomyelitis. The patient is a 14-year-old girl with Gaucher disease type 1 who presented with severe thoracolumbar pain. She was treated with a 4-week course of antibiotics for presumed osteomyelitis with clinical improvement.</AbstractText>
